  "notes": "The historic Al-Sarafiya Bridge crosses the Tigris on two high steel through-trusses and a lower central span. Open cross-bracing, pale gray lattice, red-and-white road separators, sidewalks and the long approach spans follow the photographed bridge. The model depicts the historic Al-Sarafiya crossing and approaches. The mapped relation also includes the separately built second span. Its outline remains in the source controls and its construction and future road alignment are outside this landmark replacement. Truss stations, pier dimensions, grades and painted details are exterior reconstructions from ordinary photos and the standard viewer terrain. The native river surface remains and exposed pier heights vary with the host water level.",
